# .secretignore — allowlist for scripts/scan-secrets.sh
# Created: 2026-04-19 (3-Brain Pipeline v3 Patch 1)
# Hardened: 2026-04-20 — dropped rotated-secret literal allowlists. The scanner
# no longer stores historical credential values as literal regex (per Codex review);
# generic character-class patterns catch them automatically.
#
# FORMAT (one entry per line):
#   # comment                                          — ignored
#   docs/path/file.md                                  — allowlist ALL secrets in file (dangerous)
#   docs/path/file.md::pattern-name                    — allowlist ONE pattern in ONE file (safe)
#   @pattern-name                                      — allowlist pattern globally (very dangerous)
#
# Pattern names (from scan-secrets.sh):
#   anthropic-api-key, openai-project-key, openai-standard-key,
#   google-api-key, slack-bot-token, github-pat, github-fg-pat,
#   aws-access-key, postgres-url, mongodb-url, mysql-url,
#   jwt-token, rotated-password-shape, pem-private-key, ssh-private-key

# ============================================
# Incident documentation — real historical leak references
# Credentials are DEAD (rotated 2026-04-19). These docs intentionally reference
# the leaked fingerprints as part of the incident record, and the values match the
# generic google-api-key / postgres-url patterns. Allowlist scoped to these files.
# ============================================
docs/ai-workflow/AI-HANDOFF/SECURITY-REMEDIATION-2026-04-19.md::google-api-key
docs/ai-workflow/AI-HANDOFF/SECURITY-REMEDIATION-2026-04-19.md::postgres-url
docs/ai-workflow/AI-HANDOFF/3-BRAIN-PIPELINE-PLAN-v2-2026-04-19.md::google-api-key
docs/ai-workflow/AI-HANDOFF/3-BRAIN-PIPELINE-PLAN-v3-FINAL-2026-04-19.md::google-api-key
docs/ai-workflow/AI-HANDOFF/3-BRAIN-PIPELINE-CODEX-REVIEW-BRIEFING-2026-04-19.md::google-api-key
docs/ai-workflow/AI-HANDOFF/3-BRAIN-PIPELINE-V3-PATCHES-2026-04-19.md::google-api-key
docs/ai-workflow/AI-HANDOFF/3-BRAIN-PIPELINE-V3-PATCHES-2026-04-19.md::postgres-url
docs/ai-workflow/AI-HANDOFF/OPUS-CODEX-DEBATE-3-BRAIN-PIPELINE-V3-2026-04-19.md::google-api-key
docs/ai-workflow/AI-HANDOFF/OPUS-CODEX-DEBATE-3-BRAIN-PIPELINE-V3-2026-04-19.md::postgres-url

# ============================================
# Test fixtures — fake tokens for unit tests (only add when actually needed)
# ============================================
# Example (commented until actually added):
# backend/tests/fixtures/test-admin-jwt.json::jwt-token

# Scanner self-reference - these are literal detector patterns, not keys.
scripts/scan-secrets.sh::pem-private-key
scripts/scan-secrets.sh::ssh-private-key

# Shadow-seeder gate fixtures (verified inert 2026-08-24, Fable): synthetic
# localhost/example.com URLs with placeholder passwords, used to TEST the
# refuse-non-shadow gate. Every line read before allowlisting. No real creds.
backend/scripts/seed-shadow-db.mjs::postgres-url
backend/scripts/seed-shadow-db.selftest.mjs::postgres-url
backend/scripts/seed-shadow-db.test.mjs::postgres-url
# CI throwaway-container URL (verified 2026-08-24): literal shadow:shadow@localhost,
# an ephemeral job-scoped Postgres. The header forbids real credentials here.
.github/workflows/migration-shadow-check.yml::postgres-url
# Ox Alpha hostile-review output, 2026-08-24. The reviewer quoted the CI throwaway-container
# URL back verbatim while arguing its committed bytes must be verified — same literal already
# allowlisted for the workflow and the seeder above: shadow:shadow@localhost/shadow, loopback
# only, dies with the job. Both lines read before allowlisting; no real credential present.
docs/ai-workflow/AI-HANDOFF/panel-swa200-final-2026-08-24/ox-r1.stdout.txt::postgres-url
docs/ai-workflow/AI-HANDOFF/panel-swa200-final-2026-08-24/ox-r1/OX-REVIEW-1.md::postgres-url
# shadow-gate-local.mjs, 2026-08-26. Two hits, both read before allowlisting:
#   :51  the loopback throwaway template literal (shadow:shadow@localhost:${PORT}/shadow) — the
#        same disposable-container credential already allowlisted for seed-shadow-db above
#   :161 a HELP STRING inside an error message, showing USER:PASS placeholders to the operator
# No real credential in either.
backend/scripts/shadow-gate-local.mjs::postgres-url
